# Trivy exceptions for THIRD-PARTY images KubeBolt bundles but does not build.
#
# Used ONLY by the two `preflight-third-party-scan` steps in
# .github/workflows/release.yml (victoria-metrics and vmagent). KubeBolt's own
# images — api, web, single-container — are scanned by `image-scan` against the strict
# `.trivyignore`, which stays empty of entries.
#
# The split exists because the two cases are not the same problem. When a CVE
# lands in a dependency we compile, the answer is to bump and rebuild, and the
# gate should keep failing until we do. When it lands inside a vendor's published
# binary, we cannot fix it — only wait for their rebuild or drop the dependency.
# One shared file would let the second silence the first.
#
# Every entry still needs an owner, a justification, and a remove-by date, and
# the same rule applies: this is not a way to push an urgent release out.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # YYYY-MM-DD <owner> — justification + remove-by date

# 2026-10-12: victoria-metrics and vmagent v1.153.0-scratch are built on Go
# 1.27.1 and golang.org/x/net v0.59.0, which carry the three CVEs below (all
# HIGH, all fixed in Go 1.27.2 / x/net v0.60.0). The fix ships in VictoriaMetrics
# v1.154.0, which is still a release candidate; 2.3.1 stays on the latest
# stable instead. KubeBolt's own images are rebuilt on Go 1.26.9 and x/net
# v0.60.0 and carry none of them. Remove when the pins move to v1.154.0 final.
CVE-2026-78667  # 2026-10-12 lmaina — net/http, in VictoriaMetrics' Go 1.27.1 (vendor binary). Remove by 2026-11-15.
CVE-2026-78669  # 2026-10-12 lmaina — HTTP/2, in VictoriaMetrics' Go 1.27.1 and x/net v0.59.0 (vendor binary). Remove by 2026-11-15.
CVE-2026-97031  # 2026-10-12 lmaina — crypto/tls, in VictoriaMetrics' Go 1.27.1 (vendor binary). Remove by 2026-11-15.
